          "short": "Sample answers: $1020$, $121980$, $59220$.",
          "worked": "Check divisibility by $3$ using the digit sum, by $4$ using the final two digits, and by $5$ using the final digit.\n\n$1020$ has digit sum $1+0+2+0=3$, final two digits $20$, and final digit $0$.\n\n$121980$ has digit sum $1+2+1+9+8+0=21$, final two digits $80$, and final digit $0$.\n\n$59220$ has digit sum $5+9+2+2+0=18$, final two digits $20$, and final digit $0$.\n\nThe digit sums are divisible by $3$, the final two-digit numbers are divisible by $4$, and every number ends in $0$. Thus each is divisible by $3$, $4$ and $5$. Other answers are possible.",
